<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντικαθίστημι</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντικατ-</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-καταστήσω</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>replace, substitute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.93
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ἐλάσσω ἀντικαταστῆσαι πάλιν</span>
			<i>replace</i> an equal quantity of gold, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλους ἀ.</span>
			<i>set up</i> others <i>in their stead,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				838a3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>set against, oppose,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.93
				</span></i>
			; <i>establish as a counterpart,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					591a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>set up</i> or <i>bring back again,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπὶ τὸ θαρρεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.65
				</span></i>
			; <i>rally,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς θορυβηθέντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					6.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, with aor. 2 and pf.
			
				Act.
			; also aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεστάθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					3.1.38
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be put in another's place, reign in his
				stead,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.37
			</span></i>, X.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be pitted against</i> another, <i>opposed,</i> abs., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.47
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
					7.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> in lawsuits,
				<i>to be confronted with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί, πρός τινα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				97.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				168.11
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>.</div>
